The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if ((dep->flags & DWC3_EP_PENDING_REQUEST)) {
    if (dep->flags & DWC3_EP_TRANSFER_STARTED) {
        dwc3_stop_active_transfer(dwc, dep->number, true);
        dep->flags = DWC3_EP_ENABLED;
    } else {
        u32 cur_uf;
        cur_uf = __dwc3_gadget_get_frame(dwc);
        __dwc3_gadget_start_isoc(dwc, dep, cur_uf);
        dep->flags &= ~DWC3_EP_PENDING_REQUEST;
    }
}
```
Reason:
The simplification in the handling of ISO transfers did not properly manage the conditions under which an active transfer should be stopped or started, leading to performance degradation when the XferInProgress event occurred.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if ((dep->flags & DWC3_EP_BUSY) &&
    !(dep->flags & DWC3_EP_MISSED_ISOC)) {
    WARN_ON_ONCE(!dep->resource_index);
    ret = __dwc3_gadget_kick_transfer(dep, dep->resource_index);
}
```
Reason:
The added code checks if the endpoint is busy and not missing isochronous transfers, allowing the transfer to be kicked off correctly, thus restoring the performance of ISO transfers to their original state.

